/**
 * #10868 — the web soccer match screen on REAL retained production bodies: the
 * same answers the native soccer suites pin at 274369bc
 * (`ios/Bain Luck/BainLuckTests/Soccer*10868Tests.swift`), through the web
 * authorities the event page already uses.
 *
 * FIXTURE — `soccerMatch10868.fixtures.json`, generated by
 * `/tmp/soccerweb-tools/extract.py` (outside the repo): every body is the exact
 * raw string between the native fixture's `##"""` delimiters, copied VERBATIM
 * from `SoccerRetainedAdapter10868Tests.swift` (Hull City v Everton before
 * kickoff; Real Valladolid CF v Albacete live at 4–0 and after its 5–0 final)
 * and `SoccerExactScoreAdapter10868Tests.swift` (Hull–Everton's exact-score
 * markets and its 2–2 final). The four detail bodies are byte for byte the
 * retained production captures (their native sha256 pins are re-checked below);
 * the history and markets bodies are the native fixtures' own REDUCED VERBATIM
 * SUBSETS, so an in-game interval across a left-out row is wider than served.
 *
 * CONSTRUCTED, and named where used: `now` (the native clocks); the hero pair,
 * from the page's own `resolveProbability` exactly as page.tsx calls it; the
 * owner's story admissions and exact-score descriptor (`fixtures.constructed`,
 * parsed from the native tests so the ids are the same — NO PRODUCTION OWNER
 * SUPPLIES ANY OF THEM); and one-key edits that mirror native's
 * (`F.edited`, `F.editedRow`, `F.graded`). Jest runs in UTC; clock words are
 * compared through the screen's own formatter, never a hard-coded spelling.
 *
 * PLATFORM DIFFERENCE, deliberate: a settled verdict is web's one settled
 * vocabulary (`propVerdictLabel`: HIT / MISS) where native says
 * OutcomeVerdict's "Won" / "Lost" — as web's hockey All props already does.
 */

